    "body": "## Purpose\n\nPart of #60420 (does not close it: host-backed prefills still stage).\n\nWith HiSparse, the FlashMLA sparse BF16 path stages every prefill: it copies the request's full history from host into a transient GPU buffer (`stage_prefill_rows`), even when all of its pages are GPU-resident, and joins decode and prefill outputs with `torch.cat` in mixed batches. Startup profiling doesn't cover either allocation (its dummy run is one chunk of short prefills), so a long accepted prompt can OOM a running server. The same failure was reproduced on the FlashInfer path; see #60417.\n\nFix: when every scheduled page is resident (`all_context_pages_resident`), convert all rows against resident pages and run one kernel. Host-backed prefills still stage; making that buffer accounted is tracked in #60072.\n\nIndependent of #60417. Both PRs carry the same 4-line `index_group.py` routing change (and its test case), so whichever lands second rebases trivially.\n\n`test_hisparse_mixed_batch_bf16_row_split` keeps its KV in the host pool, so it now sets `all_context_pages_resident = False` to match that scenario. The default of `True` only went unnoticed before because this path never checked the flag.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -k \"hisparse or flashmla\"` (CUDA)\n- [ ] HiSparse e2e with `--kv-cache-dtype auto` on FlashMLA sparse: long prompt + concurrent decodes, no OOM, peak memory vs main\n- [ ] GSM8K HiSparse eval on this path\n\n## Test Result\n\nPending.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
